    "result_text": "All tests pass. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required a `riskFlag` on the owner response that is `true` when **any** of three conditions hold: the owner is a possible duplicate, the email domain is disposable-adjacent, or the city is over its soft capacity.\n\nI placed each piece of logic with the concern it belongs to and reused the existing per-city / email helpers rather than re-deriving anything:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `riskFlag` boolean to the `Owner` schema (the generator produces `OwnerDto.setRiskFlag`).\n\n2. **`Emails.isDisposableAdjacent`** \u2014 a new sibling of the existing `isDisposableDomain`. \"Disposable-adjacent\" means the domain shares its **second-level label** with a known disposable provider (e.g. subdomain `x.mailinator.com` or sibling `mailinator.net`). This matters because exact disposable domains are already rejected at create time, so only these near-misses can ever reach a persisted owner.\n\n3. **`Cities.isOverSoftCapacity`** \u2014 reuses the existing `count(...)` and the `CAPACITY_WARNING_THRESHOLD` (40) that also drives the capacity warning, so both rules accumulate over one count.\n\n4. **`RiskFlag`** (new) \u2014 a tiny composite rule that ORs the three signals: the stored `possibleDuplicate` flag, `Emails.isDisposableAdjacent`, and `Cities.isOverSoftCapacity`. Each sub-check stays owned by its own class.\n\n5. **`OwnerResponses.toDto`** (new) \u2014 the three single-owner responders (`RespondWithOwner`, `RespondWithOwnerCreated`, `RespondWithOwnerUpdated`) previously each copied the same DTO-enrichment lines (bulk-signup + capacity warnings). I lifted that into one place and added `riskFlag` there, so the fix didn't turn into three copy-pasted lines and the responders no longer duplicate response assembly.\n\nFull suite: **BUILD SUCCESS**, including the new `coreRiskFlagFalseNormally` acceptance test (a structured owner \u2014 no email, unique city, unique surname \u2014 correctly reports `riskFlag: false`).",
